ITEMS=[]
def family(options,rows):
 for k,(stem,why) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((stem,[options[k]]+options[:k]+options[k+1:],why))
family(['The controlling entity','The utility owner/operator','The crane operator','The A/D director'],[
('A general contractor controls site preparation and knows of a buried tank under the proposed crane setup. Who has the specific OSHA duty to disclose that known ground hazard to the crane user and operator?','The controlling entity must disclose known subsurface hazards and ensure required ground preparation under1926.1402.'),
('A lift plan relies on a nearby power line being deenergized and visibly grounded at the worksite. From whom must that condition be confirmed?','OSHA1926.1408 requires confirmation from the utility owner/operator; appearances or assumptions do not establish deenergization.'),
('A crew member is about to enter an assembly location hidden from the controls where crane movement could injure them. Whom must the crew member inform before entering?','Under1926.1404(e), the operator must know the worker is entering that location and must not move equipment until the worker is reported safe.'),
('Before boom assembly starts, who must ensure that crew members understand their tasks, associated hazards and positions to avoid?','The assembly/disassembly director has this crew-instruction responsibility under1926.1404(d).')])
family(['A buried underground void','A nearby retaining wall','Saturated supporting soil','Recently placed loose fill'],[
('A setup drawing shows an abandoned chamber below an apparently solid paved pad. Which concealed condition most directly threatens support?','A buried void can undermine the apparent surface support;1926.1402 requires known buried hazards to be disclosed.'),
('An outrigger is proposed beside a structure holding back a large height of soil. Which site feature needs assessment for its ability to resist the added loading?','A retaining wall and the retained soil require assessment; their apparent surface condition does not establish capacity.'),
('After prolonged rain, water accumulates around a pad and the soil softens. Which changed ground condition requires reassessment?','Water accumulation and softening indicate saturated support; ground support must continue to meet manufacturer requirements.'),
('An excavated trench has just been backfilled, but no compaction assessment is available. Which condition makes its support uncertain?','Recently placed loose fill may settle under crane loads and cannot be assumed to provide adequate support.')])
family(['Increase effective bearing area','Restore the specified level','Verify concealed site hazards','Restrict the swing/crush zone'],[
('An engineered support plan calls for larger mats to spread each outrigger reaction over the soil. What is the primary purpose of the larger mat footprint?','Effective bearing area spreads reaction over more ground; the complete support system must still be suitable.'),
('A supported crane is outside the manufacturer’s allowable tilt. Which setup objective must be achieved before lifting?','The crane must meet the manufacturer’s degree-of-level requirement, not merely have sufficient mat area.'),
('A paved setup area has no visible damage, but records may show old tanks and utilities beneath it. Which action addresses that unresolved issue?','Reviewing known subsurface hazards addresses what cannot be judged from surface appearance alone.'),
('The rotating counterweight can trap a worker against a fence. Which work-area action addresses this specific hazard?','Control lines, warning lines or similar barriers restrict access to the swing/crush hazard area under1926.1424.')])
family(['4 feet of clearance','6 feet of clearance','10 feet of clearance','16 feet of clearance'],[
('Under OSHA Table T, a crane travels on a construction site with no load beneath a 0.5kV AC line. What is the listed minimum clearance, with all other travel safeguards still required?','Table T specifies4ft for unloaded travel at voltages up to0.75kV.'),
('An unloaded construction-site crane travels near a 25kV AC line. What minimum clearance does OSHA Table T specify?','Table T specifies6ft for more than0.75kV through50kV; this is an unloaded-travel rule, not a lifting clearance.'),
('For unloaded construction-site travel near a 230kV AC line, what minimum clearance is listed in OSHA Table T?','Table T specifies10ft for more than50kV through345kV.'),
('A crane travels without a load near a 500kV AC line on a construction site. Which Table T clearance applies?','Table T specifies16ft for more than345kV through750kV; all required travel precautions also apply.')])
family(['An elevated warning boundary','A continuously communicating spotter','A movement-limiting device','A utility deenergization confirmation'],[
('Under a power-line encroachment plan, what provides the visible flagged boundary that the operator must not cross?','An elevated warning line, barricade or line of signs marks the prescribed boundary under1926.1408(b)(3).'),
('During unloaded travel within20ft of a line, which measure supplies timely distance information directly to the driver?','A dedicated spotter in continuous contact gauges clearance and provides timely information under1926.1411.'),
('Which listed power-line control physically limits the crane’s range of movement rather than merely warning the operator?','A movement-limiting device prevents entering the restricted range when properly set; an alarm only warns.'),
('Which listed evidence supports the plan’s claim that a line has been deenergized and visibly grounded at the worksite?','The required condition must be confirmed by the utility owner/operator; boundaries and spotters do not establish it.')])
family(['Overall transport height','Overall transport width','Ground-support capacity','Counterweight swing clearance'],[
('A crane’s access route passes beneath a low, non-electrical bridge. Which equipment dimension must be compared with the bridge opening?','Transport height determines vertical physical clearance; electrical-line rules are separate.'),
('The access route passes between fixed gateposts. Which equipment dimension primarily determines whether the crane fits through the opening?','Transport width must fit the usable gate opening with the required safe clearances.'),
('The route crosses an area of soft fill with no overhead or side obstruction. Which site property needs verification before travel?','The route must support the crane; adequate geometric clearance does not establish bearing capacity.'),
('At the final setup, the carrier fits beside a wall, but the upperworks will rotate. Which additional clearance must be assessed?','Counterweight swing clearance determines whether rotation creates collision and pinch/crush hazards.')])
family(['20 square feet','25 square feet','30 square feet','40 square feet'],[
('For a simplified planning calculation only, a mat carries40,000lb uniformly over soil assigned an allowable2,000lb/ft². What minimum effective area follows from load divided by allowable pressure?','40,000/2,000=20ft². Actual support design must also address mat strength, load distribution and site conditions.'),
('A rectangular mat has an effective supported footprint5ft by5ft. What area enters a simplified uniform-bearing calculation?','5×5=25ft²; nominal mat size alone does not prove that its full area is effective.'),
('A preliminary support plan requires20ft² of effective area plus a specified10ft² allowance. What total area does that plan require?','The stated areas add to30ft². This is arithmetic using the supplied plan, not a universal safety allowance.'),
('An original mat provides20ft². A revised engineered plan explicitly calls for twice that effective area. What area is required?','Twice20ft² is40ft²; only the stated plan establishes the increase.')])
family(['Site as-built drawings','Manufacturer setup instructions','A geotechnical support assessment','A coordination communication plan'],[
('Which record is most directly useful for locating previously constructed underground tanks or utilities beneath a proposed pad?','As-built drawings may document buried structures; the controlling entity must disclose known hazards.'),
('Which source specifies the crane’s permitted outrigger deployment and degree of level for the intended configuration?','Manufacturer instructions define permitted setup; site documents do not replace equipment limits.'),
('Which document most directly evaluates whether the soil and supporting arrangement can carry the proposed reactions?','A geotechnical/support assessment addresses ground bearing; equipment charts alone do not establish soil capacity.'),
('Two cranes have overlapping working radii. Which arrangement specifically addresses how their operations will be coordinated?','OSHA1926.1424(b) requires a coordination system when cranes’ working areas overlap.')])
family(['Lower the travel boom','Illuminate the line location','Account for terrain movement','Identify a safe travel path'],[
('Before unloaded travel under a line, the boom is higher than necessary for transport. Which action addresses the equipment’s travel height?','OSHA1926.1411 requires lowering the boom/mast sufficiently to maintain the specified travel clearances.'),
('An unloaded crane must travel near lines at night, and their position cannot be seen. Which added precaution directly makes the line location identifiable?','In poor visibility, lines must be illuminated or another means must identify their location.'),
('A travel route includes a dip and a raised crossing that can make the boom move relative to a line. Which factor must the clearance plan explicitly include?','Speed and terrain can change equipment position and must not cause a clearance breach.'),
('In poor visibility, the driver can see the line but has not been given a verified route around obstacles. Which further precaution is required?','OSHA1926.1411 requires identifying and using a safe travel path as well as identifying the lines.')])
family(['Support before pin removal','Verify the assist-crane loads','Protect synthetic sling edges','Confirm crew members are clear'],[
('A lattice-boom section will become unstable when its connecting pins are removed. Which preparation directly controls that movement?','Boom components must be rigged or supported to maintain stability when pins are removed under1926.1404(h)(7).'),
('An assist crane will carry changing loads during several assembly phases. What must be established for each phase before assembly begins?','The loads imposed on the assist crane must be verified before assembly/disassembly under1926.1404(h)(4).'),
('A synthetic sling contacts a sharp boom-component edge during assembly. Which measure directly protects the sling from this condition?','Synthetic slings must be protected from sharp or abrasive edges and harmful configurations under1926.1404(r).'),
('The operator knows a worker entered an assembly position hidden from view. What confirmation is needed before moving the affected equipment?','The pre-arranged communication system must confirm the worker is in a safe position before movement resumes.')])
family(['Under the jack float or pad','At the approved boom support points','At the identified lifting points','Across the designated hazard boundary'],[
('For a jack-equipped outrigger, where must the supporting blocking be placed under OSHA’s outrigger rule?','Blocking belongs under the float/pad of the jack, not beneath an arbitrary point on the beam.'),
('Where should blocking supporting a lattice-boom section be positioned to avoid structural damage and dangerous collapse?','Appropriate support locations protect structural integrity and prevent movement; follow the assembly procedures.'),
('When a boom component is hoisted during assembly, where should its handling rigging attach?','Suitable designated lifting points prevent structural damage and allow controlled handling under1926.1404(h)(5).'),
('Where should a warning line restricting entry into the counterweight pinch/crush area be established?','The warning line marks the boundary of the designated hazard area under1926.1424.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==44
